>west
The big cats suddenly spring out of their slumber, and begin moving stealthily around the den, as if in preparation for a feeding.

Lions' Den
Here inside the round cage you stand in a dingy indoor twilight, surrounded by a panorama of closely spaced bars. The cage door that you're still keeping an eye on is to the east.

Built into the southern side of the round cage there is a square grate which is lowered, blocking some sort of passage.

A lion stand sits here.

>examine the lions
You glance at each lion and realize that, because you were outside the big top stuck waiting in line when the lions were introduced, you're not certain who is who. You'll have to refer to each as the shaggy lion or the smooth-bodied lion.

Both lions continue pacing nervously back and forth around the den, never letting you out of their sight.

>whip smooth lion
As the whip cracks just inches above the smooth-bodied lion's hide, the puzzled animal scratches to a halt in front of the grate. Leaning back on its haunches, the lion flexes its forepaws.

The shaggy lion keeps pacing nervously back and forth around the den, never letting you out of its sight.

>whip smooth lion
"Snap!" The lion performs an obedient roll-over, flecking its hide with sawdust.

The shaggy lion keeps pacing nervously back and forth around the den, never letting you out of its sight.

>whip smooth lion
The smooth-bodied lion cowers, does a couple of nervous pirouettes, then jaunts off to the side of the lions' den where it hunkers down and lets out a huge yawn.

The shaggy lion keeps pacing nervously back and forth around the den, never letting you out of its sight.

>lift grate
Using the stool as a barrier against the shaggy lion, you're able to reach it. The rusty grate slides up, jamming into place. 

The shaggy lion keeps pacing nervously back and forth around the den, never letting you out of its sight.

>throw meat in passage
You fling the corpuscular lump of meat into the darkness of the passage. The lions seem eager to go after the meat, but your presence here is making them hesitate.

The shaggy lion keeps pacing nervously back and forth around the den, never letting you out of its sight.

>east
As you exit the den, the lions slink out through the open grate.

